                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simply+connected+topological+space"} simply connected
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibers"} fibers
              are identified with a typical fiber
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
              up to
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+homotopy+equivalence"} weak homotopy equivalence
              by connectedness (
              %a{:href => "Introduction+to+Stable+homotopy+theory+--+P#FibersOfSerreFibrations"}> this example
              ), and well-defined up to unique iso in the homotopy category by simply-connectedness:
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
