                  %mo =
                  %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F = \ast
            is given by a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Steenrod+square"} Steenrod square
            operation
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi d
                    %mn 3
                  %mo =
                  %msup
                    %mi Sq
                    %mn 3
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  d_3 = Sq^3
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#AtiyahHirzebruch61"}> Atiyah-Hirzebruch 61
            ).
          %p
            For
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+K-theory"} twisted K-theory
            this picks up in addition the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cup+product"} cup product
            with the 3-class
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
            of the twist:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi d
                    %mn 3
                  %mo =
                  %msup
                    %mi Sq
                    %mn 3
                  %mo +
                  %mi H
                  %mo ∪
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  d_3 = Sq^3 + H \cup(-)
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#Rosenberg82"}> Rosenberg 82
            ,
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#AtiyahSegal05"} Atiyah-Segal 05 (4.1)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi d
                    %mn 5
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d_5
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi d
                    %mn 7
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d_7
            here are given by higher
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Massey+products"} Massey products
            with the twisting class (
            %a{:href => "#AtiyahSegal05"}> Atiyah-Segal 05 sections 5-7
            ).
          %h3#ApplicationDBraneChargesInStringTheory D-brane charges in string theory
          %p
            In
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+theory"} string theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D-brane+charges"} D-brane charges
            are classes in
            = succeed "-cohomology," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                    %mo =
                    %mi KU
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E = KU
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K-theory"} K-theory
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#ForKTheory"} above
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %mo =
                  %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F = \ast
            hence expresses ordinary cohomology in all even or all odd degrees, and being in the kernel of all the differentials is hence the constraint on such ordinary cohomology data to lift to genuine K-theory classes, hence to genuine D-brane charges. In this way the Atiyah-Hirzebruch spectral sequences is used in (
            %a{:href => "#MaldacenaMooreSeiberg01"}> Maldacena-Moore-Seiberg 01
            ,
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#EvslinSati06"} Evslin-Sati 06
          %h2#references References
          %h3#general General
          %p
            The statement of the existence of the spectral sequence first appears in print (with
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                  %mo =
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E =
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+K-theory"} topological K-theory
          %ul
            %li#AtiyahHirzebruch61
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M.+F.+Atiyah"}> M. F. Atiyah
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/F.+Hirzebruch"} F. Hirzebruch
              = succeed "," do
                %em Vector bundles and homogeneous spaces
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "http://hirzebruch.mpim-bonn.mpg.de/87/"} web
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1142/9789814401319_0008"} doi:10.1142/9789814401319_0008
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://www.ams.org/mathscinet-getitem?mr=0139181"} MR 0139181
          %p but the proof given consists essentially in pointing to section XV.7 (“a more general setting in which the theory of spectral sequences may be developed”) of
          %ul
            %li#CartanEilenberg56
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Henri+Cartan"}> Henri Cartan
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Samuel+Eilenberg"} Samuel Eilenberg
              = succeed "," do
                %em Homological algebra
          %p
            This is by filtering over the stages of the base space CW-complex. That one gets an isomorphic spectral sequence by instead filtering over the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Postnikov+tower"} Postnikov tower
            of any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Omega-spectrum"} Omega-spectrum
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Brown+representability+theorem"} representing
            the given
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+%28Eilenberg-Steenrod%29+cohomology"} generalized cohomology
            theory is due to
          %ul
            %li#Maunder63
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/C.+R.+F.+Maunder"}> C. R. F. Maunder
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em The spectral sequence of an extraordinary cohomology theory
              %strong 59
              3 (1963) 567- 574
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [
              %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1017/S0305004100037245"} doi:10.1017/S0305004100037245
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ]
          %p Early lecture notes:
          %ul
            %li#Adams74
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Frank+Adams"}> Frank Adams
              , part III section 7 of
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stable+homotopy+and+generalised+homology"} Stable homotopy and generalised homology
          %p
            where the idea is attributed to
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/George+Whitehead"} George Whitehead
          %blockquote
            %p
              the Atiyah-Hirzebruch spectral sequence, which was really invented by G. W. Whitehead but not published by him (
              %a{:href => "#Adams74"}> Adams 74, p. 127-128
              )
            %p
              These spectral sequences were probably first invented by G. W. Whitehead, but he got them just after he wrote the paper
              = succeed "Whitehead" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ]
              in which they ought to have appeared. They then became a folk-theorem and were eventually published by Atiyah and Hirzebruch (
              %a{:href => "#Adams74"}> Adams 74, p. 215
              )
          %p A more detailed account of the proof is in
          %ul
            %li#Kochman96
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stanley+Kochman"}> Stanley Kochman
              , theorem 4.2.5 of
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bordism%2C+Stable+Homotopy+and+Adams+Spectral+Sequences"} Bordism, Stable Homotopy and Adams Spectral Sequences
          %p
            Further discussion of the case of
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+K-theory"} twisted K-theory
          %ul
            %li#Rosenberg82
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jonathan+Rosenberg"}> Jonathan Rosenberg
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    Homological Invariants of Extensions of
                    = succeed "-algebras" do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %msup
                              %mi C
                              %mo *
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^\ast
            %li#AtiyahSegal05
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Atiyah"}> Michael Atiyah
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Graeme+Segal"} Graeme Segal
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Twisted K-theory and cohomology
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0510674"} arXiv:math/0510674
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dale+Husem%C3%B6ller"}> Dale Husemöller
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Joachim"} Michael Joachim
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Branislav+Jur%C4%8Do"} Branislav Jurčo
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Martin+Schottenloher"} Martin Schottenloher
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Basic+Bundle+Theory+and+K-Cohomology+Invariants"} Basic Bundle Theory and K-Cohomology Invariants
                = succeed "," do
                  %strong 726
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.mathematik.uni-muenchen.de/~schotten/Texte/978-3-540-74955-4_Book_LNP726.pdf"} pdf
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://link.springer.com/book/10.1007/978-3-540-74956-1"} doi:10.1007/978-3-540-74956-1
          %p
            An analogous spectral sequence for higher
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+de+Rham+cohomology"} twisted de Rham cohomology
            is discussed in
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "twisted+de+Rham+cohomology#LiLiuWang09"} Li, Liu &amp; Wang 2009
          %p
            A discussion of the
            = succeed "-AHSS" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mapping+spectra"} mapping spectra
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [X,-]
            into the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Postnikov+tower"} Postnikov tower
            is due to
          %ul
            %li#Shulman13
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mike+Shulman"}> Mike Shulman
              ,
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/homotopytypetheory/show/spectral+sequences"} spectral sequences
              (2013)
          %h3#EquivariantVersion Equivariant version
          %p
            Discussion of the AHSS in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bredon+cohomology"} Bredon
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+stable+homotopy+theory"} equivariant stable homotopy theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+cohomology"} equivariant cohomology
            includes
          %ul
            %li#DavisLueck98
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/James+Davis"}> James Davis
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Wolfgang+Lueck"} Wolfgang Lueck
              = succeed "," do
                %em Spaces over a category and assembly maps in isomorphism conjectures in K- and L-theory
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "http://www.indiana.edu/~jfdavis/papers/assembly.pdf"} pdf
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://www.math.uiuc.edu/K-theory/0131/"} K-Theory archive
          %p
            Discussion in genuine equivariant cohomology, i.e. including
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/RO%28G%29-grading"} RO(G)-grading
          %ul
            %li#Kronholm10
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/William+Kronholm"}> William Kronholm
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  The
                  = succeed "-graded" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi RO
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi G
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} RO(G)
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "http://www.swarthmore.edu/NatSci/wkronho1/serre.pdf"} pdf
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://projecteuclid.org/euclid.hha/1296223823"} Euclid
          %h3#examples Examples
          %p
            Application for the case of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K-theory"} K-theory
            to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D-brane+charges"} D-brane charges
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+theory"} string theory
            is discussed in
          %ul
            %li#MaldacenaMooreSeiberg01
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Juan+Maldacena"}> Juan Maldacena
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gregory+Moore"} Gregory Moore
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Nathan+Seiberg"} Nathan Seiberg
                = succeed "," do
                  %em D-Brane Instantons and K-Theory Charges
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0108100"} arXiv:hep-th/0108100
            %li#EvslinSati06
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jarah+Evslin"}> Jarah Evslin
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hisham+Sati"} Hisham Sati
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Can D-Branes Wrap Nonrepresentable Cycles?
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0607045"} arXiv:hep-th/0607045
          %p and detailed review of this is in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Fabio+Ruffino"}> Fabio Ruffino
              ,
              %em Topics on topology and superstring theory
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0910.4524"}> arXiv:0910.4524
              )
          %p
            Discussion for the
            = succeed "-equivariant" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}/2
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KR+cohomology+theory"} KR cohomology theory
            (relevant for D-branes in
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orientifolds"} orientifolds
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Daniel+Dugger"}> Daniel Dugger
              ,
              %em An Atiyah-Hirzebruch spectral sequence for KR-theory
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0304099"} arXiv:math/0304099
          %p
            Discussion for the case of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Morava+K-theory"} Morava K-theory
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Morava+E-theory"} Morava E-theory
            with comments on application to charges of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-branes"} M-branes
            is in
          %ul
            %li#SatiWesterland11
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hisham+Sati"}> Hisham Sati
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Craig+Westerland"} Craig Westerland
              %em Twisted Morava K-theory and E-theory
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1109.3867"}> arXiv:1109.3867
              )
          %p
            Application to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/motivic+homotopy+theory"} motivic
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cobordism+cohomology+theory"} cobordism cohomology theory
            is discussed in
          %ul
            %li
              Nobuaki Yagita,
              %em Applications of the Atiyah-Hirzebruch spectral sequences for motivic cobordisms
              (
              %a{:href => "http://www.math.uiuc.edu/K-theory/0627/ah.pdf"}> pdf
              )
          %p
            Application to the
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K-theory+classification+of+topological+phases+of+matter"} K-theory classification of topological phases of matter
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ken+Shiozaki"}> Ken Shiozaki
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Masatoshi+Sato"} Masatoshi Sato
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kiyonori+Gomi"} Kiyonori Gomi
              = succeed "," do
                %em Atiyah-Hirzebruch Spectral Sequence in Band Topology: General Formalism and Topological Invariants for 230 Space Groups
              %strong 106
              (2022) 165103 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1802.06694"}> arXiv:1802.06694
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevB.106.165103"} doi:10.1103/PhysRevB.106.165103
        .revisedby
          %p
            Last revised on July  9, 2023 at 18:05:30.
